# ordin-obs, OBS Recorder Adapter: records a meeting's sound with OBS on this computer
error-obs-already-recording = OBS is already recording. Stop that recording in OBS first.
error-obs-not-installed = To record meetings, install OBS, the free recording program, then come back here.
error-obs-not-reachable = Open OBS, then open the WebSocket settings in its Tools menu and tick the box that turns WebSocket on.
error-obs-not-recording = OBS isn't recording.
error-obs-output-missing = Ordin couldn't find the recording OBS made.
error-obs-password-needed = Paste the OBS password: in OBS, open the WebSocket settings in the Tools menu, choose Show Connect Info and copy the password.
error-obs-password-refused = OBS didn't accept the password. Copy it again: in OBS, open the WebSocket settings in the Tools menu and choose Show Connect Info.
error-obs-port-invalid = Choose a port number from 1024 to 65535.
error-obs-request-failed = OBS didn't do what Ordin asked. Try again.
error-obs-scene-failed = Ordin couldn't set up its meeting scene in OBS. Try again.
error-obs-timeout = OBS didn't answer. Try again.
error-obs-version-unsupported = Ordin needs OBS 28 or later. Update OBS, then try again.
